            "instructions": "<ol><li>Remove the pit from the umezuke and place it in a blender with the soy sauce, maple syrup, garlic powder, and grated ginger.</li><li>Blend for about 20 seconds, until the ume is finely incorporated and the sauce is smooth.</li><li>Pour the mixture into a small saucepan and bring it to a gentle simmer over medium-low heat.</li><li>Cook for 3–5 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the flavors are combined and the sauce has slightly thickened.</li><li>Remove from the heat and allow the sauce to cool. It will continue to thicken slightly as it cools.</li></ol>",
